--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LZMA SDK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The LZMA decoder is vendored from the LZMA SDK and lives in
third_party/lzma-sdk/ (LzmaDec.c, LzmaDec.h, 7zTypes.h, Precomp.h,
Compiler.h). Those files are incorporated unmodified and remain subject to
their own terms; the source files carry the SPDX identifier LZMA-SDK-9.22.
Provenance and per-file checksums are recorded in third_party/lzma-sdk/README.md.

  LZMA SDK is placed in the public domain by its author, Igor Pavlov.
  Where a copy of the 7-Zip licence is retained in the distribution, its terms
  continue to apply to those files.

The SDK is also the historical origin of the BSDIFF43 `offtin` sign-magnitude
integer encoding used by the delta format.
